Short:        Free MUI replacement for OS 3.x
Author:       Tobias Karlsson
Type:         util/libs
Version:      [RELEASE] - [STAGE]
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.1
Requires:     AmigaOS 3.1+, 68000+, Installer 43+

OpenMUI is a free, open-source replacement for MUI on AmigaOS 3.x. It
provides muimaster.library, the built-in classes and a preferences
program, and runs programs written for MUI 3, 4 and 5. It needs OS 3.1
or newer, a 68000 or better and no FPU. Its look and memory use follow
MUI 3.8.

OpenMUI is not MUI and is not affiliated with MUI's authors. MUI was
created by Stefan Stuntz; MUI 4 and 5 come from the MUI team. MUI was
studied black-box only: its behaviour was measured and its public
documentation read; its code was never read or copied.

Version [STAGE] ([RELEASE]), public beta.

Contents
--------
- muimaster.library [VERSION]. The file keeps MUI's name and version
  numbers because programs depend on them.
- About 45 rarely used classes and library parts as separate files in
  LIBS:OpenMUI, loaded the first time a program needs one.
- OpenMUI preferences (SYS:Prefs/OpenMUI), with an import of MUI 3.8
  settings.
- [PLUGINS] bundled MUI classes with their preference pages: NList,
  NListtree, TextEditor, BetterString, TheBar, Busy, Listtree and others.
- UP-MCC 1.0: eleven flat-look classes (UP-Button, UP-Text, UP-Panel,
  UP-Tabs, UP-Balance, UP-Slider, UP-Progress, UP-Cycle, UP-Field,
  UP-Scroller, UP-List), UP-MCC.mcp, up-mcc.library, the Inter font and
  the Dark and Light themes.
- Swedish catalogs, an SDK with examples, the user guide, developer guide,
  programmer reference and changelog (Docs/OpenMUI), and the full source.

Which MUI a program gets
------------------------
A program written for MUI 3 sees MUI 3.8 (19.35), one asking for MUI 4
sees MUI 4, one asking for MUI 5 sees MUI 5 (21.227). In OpenMUI
preferences, System page, "MUI version": "Behave as" Automatic (default),
MUI 3.8, MUI 4 or MUI 5 for all programs, plus a list of programs with a
MUI of their own. Many MUI 4/5 programs ask for version 19 and so get
MUI 3.8 under Automatic: give such a program MUI 5 in the list.

Installing
----------
Double-click Install (Installer 43 or newer; on OS 3.1 use Installer 43.3
from Aminet). The installer:
- looks for an existing MUI (3.x, 4 or 5, its MUI: assign, its
  S:User-Startup lines, every muimaster.library in LIBS:) and changes
  none of it. OpenMUI goes into the first LIBS: drawer, where programs
  find it before MUI. S:Startup-Sequence and S:User-Startup are not
  changed;
- keeps every file it replaces and records every file it installs, in
  SYS:OpenMUI/Data;
- installs a bundled class only if you have no same or newer version;
- keeps OpenMUI's settings (ENVARC:OpenMUI) on an update and does not
  touch MUI's (ENVARC:MUI).
Novice, Intermediate and Expert levels and pretend mode work.

Drawers: LIBS:OpenMUI (classes), ENVARC:OpenMUI and ENV:OpenMUI
(settings), SYS:Prefs/OpenMUI, SYS:OpenMUI (switch and uninstall icons).

Switching and removing
----------------------
SYS:OpenMUI has "Use real MUI" and "Use OpenMUI" (when a real MUI was
found) and "Uninstall". "Use real MUI" puts OpenMUI's files aside and your
own back; after a reboot programs get your MUI. "Uninstall" deletes
OpenMUI's files and restores every file of yours it replaced. From a
Shell: SYS:OpenMUI/Data/OpenMUISwitch MUI|OPENMUI|UNINSTALL|STATUS.

Performance
-----------
Cycle-exact FS-UAE emulation of an A1200 (68EC020), OS 3.1, 4 MB fast
RAM; MUI 5 on OS 3.2.1. Not measured on a real Amiga.

                           OpenMUI    MUI 3.8     MUI 5
 MUI-Demo, first program   428.2 KB   460.3 KB    1,293.7 KB
 each further program      193.1 KB   210.6-218.9 KB  427-435 KB

 ms per operation          OpenMUI    MUI 3.8     MUI 5
 application + windows     183-189    235-236     578-587 *
 window open + close       398        520-523     1,027-1,041 *
 button click              16.6       22.3        21.2 *
 string, one key           6.7        7.5-7.9     15.4 *
 list insert, 1,000 rows   248        6,652       20,253 *
 (* MUI 5 column: OpenMUI measured 236-250, 481, 17.7, 7.6 and 477
 against it in the same session.)

OpenMUI is as fast as MUI 3.8 or faster in 24 of 26 common operations
and faster than MUI 5 in all 27. It runs on a 68000 with OS 3.1.

Compatibility
-------------
Tested in emulators against real MUI 3.8 and MUI 5 with 184 programs and
class demos (YAM, AmIRC, AmFTP, IBrowse, SimpleMail, NList, TextEditor,
TheBar and others). 19 of MUI's 27 demo windows are pixel-identical to
MUI 3.8. Known differences: Docs/OpenMUI/DeveloperGuide.txt.
Reports: https://github.com/creep-ltx/openmui/issues

Origins and credits
-------------------
Zune: the MUI-compatible GUI toolkit of AROS, The AROS Development Team.
Zune68: Zune ported to AmigaOS 3 by Stefan Reinauer.
OpenMUI: the lean edition of Zune68, rewritten for 68000-class machines.
Bundled classes keep their authors' names and licences (see Source and
Docs). UP-MCC is by spotUP (https://github.com/spotUP/selecta), MIT.

